{title: Christ the Lord Is Risen Today}
{artist: Charles Wesley}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
[C]Christ the Lord is [G]risen to[C]day, [F]Alle[C]lu[G]ia!
[C]Sons of men and [G]angels [C]say, [F]Alle[C]lu[G]ia!
[C]Raise your joys and [F]triumphs [C]high, [G]Alle[C]lu[G]ia!
[C]Sing, ye heavens, and [F]earth re[C]ply, [F]Alle[C]lu[G]ia!

Verse 2
[C]Love's redeeming work is [G]done, Alleluia! [F]Fought
[C]the fight, the battle [G]won, [C]Alleluia! [F]Lo!
[C]the Sun's eclipse is [F]o'er, [C]Alleluia! [G]Lo!
[C]He sets in blood [F]no more, [F]Alleluia!

Verse 3
[C]Vain the stone, the [G]watch, the [F]seal,
[C]Alleluia! Christ hath burst [G]the [C]gates [F]of
[C]hell, Alleluia! Death in [F]vain [C]forbids [G]His
[C]rise, Alleluia! Christ hath [F]opened paradise, [F]Alleluia!

Verse 4
[C]Lives again our glorious [G]King, Alleluia! [F]Where,
[C]O death, is now [G]thy [C]sting? [F]Alleluia!
[C]Once He died our [F]souls [C]to [G]save,
[C]Alleluia! Where thy victory, [F]O grave? [F]Alleluia!

Verse 5
[C]Soar we now where Christ [G]hath led, [F]Alleluia!
[C]Following our exalted Head, [G]Alleluia! [C]Made [F]like
[C]Him, like Him we [F]rise, [C]Alleluia! [G]Ours
[C]the cross, the grave, [F]the skies, [F]Alleluia!
